    "attack_id": "T1486",
    "variation": "001",
    "name": "AWS KMS Ransomware Attack",
    "description": "Attacker creates their own KMS key, re-encrypts an S3 bucket with the attacker-controlled key using PutBucketEncryption, then schedules deletion and disables the victim's original KMS key to make data irrecoverable without paying ransom",
